{"name":"Cardinal","hex":"#c41e3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cardinal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A player on the St. Louis Cardinals team.","A player on the Arizona Cardinals team."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A player on a sports team at Stanford University."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cardinal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardinal (Catholic Church)","blocks":[{"text":"A cardinal is a senior member of the clergy of the Catholic Church. As titular members of the clergy of the Diocese of Rome, they serve as advisors to the pope, who is the bishop of Rome and the visible head of the worldwide Catholic Church. Cardinals are chosen and formally created by the pope, and typically hold the title for life. Collectively, they constitute the College of Cardinals. The most solemn responsibility of the cardinals is to elect a new pope in a conclave when the Holy See is vacant. With a few historical exceptions, popes are elected from among the College of Cardinals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Template-Cardinal_%28Bishop%29.svg/330px-Template-Cardinal_%28Bishop%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_(Catholic_Church)","wikidata":"Q45722"},{"title":"College of Cardinals","blocks":[{"text":"The College of Cardinals, also called the Sacred College of Cardinals, is the body of all cardinals of the Catholic Church. As of 3 August 2026, there are 240 cardinals, of whom 116 are eligible to vote in a conclave to elect a new pope. Appointed by the pope, cardinals serve for life, but become ineligible to participate in a conclave if they turn 80 before a papal vacancy occurs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Cardinals_in_red_vestments_during_the_funeral_mass_for_Pope_Francis_in_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Cardinals_in_red_vestments_during_the_funeral_mass_for_Pope_Francis_in_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/College_of_Cardinals","wikidata":"Q852242"},{"title":"Cardinal (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Cardinal is one of the most common surnames among aboriginal people in Canada. It originated as a French name and came to New France and was part of the North American fur trade by the 1680s. In the 1780s, a small group of Cardinals came from Quebec to what is now northern Alberta to work in the fur trade, they stayed and intermarried with the local native peoples and reproduced prolifically. As a result, thousands of Cree and Métis people from across Alberta and beyond can trace their descent to the Cardinals. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["A.W. Cardinal, Canadian musician","Aurèle Cardinal, Canadian architect","Brian Cardinal, American basketball player","Celeigh Cardinal, Canadian musician","Douglas Cardinal, Canadian architect","Fernando Cardinal, Portuguese futsal player","Gil Cardinal, Canadian architect of Métis descent","Harold Cardinal (1945–2005), Cree writer and political leader","Imajyn Cardinal, Canadian actress","Jean-Guy Cardinal, Québécois politician","Joseph-Narcisse Cardinal, Lower Canadian politician and rebel","Judah ben Isaac Cardinal, Arabic-Hebrew translator","Linda Cardinal, Canadian political scientist","Lorne Cardinal, Canadian actor","Marie Cardinal (1929–2001), French novelist","Martin Cardinal, Canadian police officer and subject of controversy","Mark Cardinal, Canadian rugby player","Mike Cardinal, Canadian politician","Tantoo Cardinal, Canadian actress"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_(surname)","wikidata":"Q16865371"},{"title":"Cardinal (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cardinal is a vivid red, which may get its name from the cassocks worn by Catholic cardinals. The cardinal bird also takes its name from the cardinal bishops."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Northern_Cardinal_-_bird_%28Cardinalis_cardinalis%29.JPG/330px-Northern_Cardinal_-_bird_%28Cardinalis_cardinalis%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_(color)","wikidata":"Q1426821"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Gesupietrochiave.jpg/500px-Gesupietrochiave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Gesupietrochiave.jpg/500px-Gesupietrochiave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGesupietrochiave.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Richelieu%2C_por_Philippe_de_Champaigne_%28detalle%29.jpg/500px-Richelieu%2C_por_Philippe_de_Champaigne_%28detalle%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Richelieu%2C_por_Philippe_de_Champaigne_%28detalle%29.jpg/500px-Richelieu%2C_por_Philippe_de_Champaigne_%28detalle%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinal Richelieu, chief minister of France in the early 17th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARichelieu%2C_por_Philippe_de_Champaigne_(detalle).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Theodor_Kardinal_Innitzer_-001-.jpg/500px-Theodor_Kardinal_Innitzer_-001-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Theodor_Kardinal_Innitzer_-001-.jpg/500px-Theodor_Kardinal_Innitzer_-001-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinal Innitzer, Archbishop of Vienna and Cardinal-Priest of San Crisogono, pictured in the early 1930s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATheodor_Kardinal_Innitzer_-001-.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Vetements_cardinal_Gamarelli.jpg/500px-Vetements_cardinal_Gamarelli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Vetements_cardinal_Gamarelli.jpg/500px-Vetements_cardinal_Gamarelli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Choir dress of a cardinal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVetements_cardinal_Gamarelli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Card._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png/500px-Card._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Card._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png/1280px-Card._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Card._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png/500px-Card._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Giovanni Battista Re served as the Dean of the College of Cardinals from 2020 to 2026","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACard._Re_WIKIPEDIA.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Cardinal_Thomas_Wolsey.jpg/500px-Cardinal_Thomas_Wolsey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Cardinal_Thomas_Wolsey.jpg/500px-Cardinal_Thomas_Wolsey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinal-priest Thomas Wolsey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal_Thomas_Wolsey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/El_cardenal_Reginald_Pole%2C_por_Sebastiano_del_Piombo.jpg/500px-El